      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Toxic agent unknown (NC State: unknown). NC State rates severity low, names cats, dogs and children, mouth and stomach irritation if eaten and contact dermatitis from the sap; RHS lists it as a skin allergen. The ASPCA page read is for Tradescantia fluminensis (spelled 'flumeninsis' on the page), a close relative, so the skin entries for pets are from_knowledge_verify. Symptom mapping 'stomach irritation' to vomiting is the agent's. Temperature 65 to 75 F is NC State; humidity: ordinary indoor air is fine, no number."
      },
